            <div xml:id="d886">

                <pb facs="1180" n="1166" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1166"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.0146/8–2844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-28T14:00:00+07:00">August 28, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 28—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1464. Soong asked me on August 24 for information as to progress in regard to
                    suggested three-power conference on the question of administration of liberated
                    areas in Far East (ReEmbs 1289, July 25 and ReDepts 1036, August 3).</p>
                <p>Soong asked me to inquire on progress and said he attached importance to early
                    development of this matter. It is probable that Generalissimo is presses [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">pressing</hi>] him in regard to it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
